1. Her father, referred to as "papa elia," speaks German and would be proud of her German pronunciation. (Verbatim: "my german pronunciation is good papa elia would be happy")

2. She wishes she had learned German properly and would like to learn it more commonly, but is currently focusing on learning Japanese. (Verbatim: "i wish i wish i learned german properly papa elia speaks german i cannot um i wish i wish i wish it was taught i wish it was taught here very like more commonly but here they usually teach french or spanish so so yeah yeah yeah i would i would i would i would love to to learn it better but i'm in the process of learning japanese")

3. She was taught French in school due to timetable clashes and did not have a choice in the language she studied. (Verbatim: "i was taught french in school i did not have a choice actually because of the timetable clashes that um yeah timetable clashes that occurred")

