5. She associates Christmas with drinking, particularly champagne with her grandmother "Nana Elia," who drinks champagne and gets giggly. (Verbatim: "only one person drinks at christmas in in my family by the way um which is nana elia nana elia will have champagne um yeah we'll have champagne and and get really giggly")

6. She has received wine as a Christmas bonus from her workplace in past years and still has unopened bottles stored in her cupboard. (Verbatim: "i've known some workplaces that will give you wine as your christmas bonus instead of an actual bonus... i actually have some bottle of wines that i've got from work from years and years and years ago")

7. She is unfamiliar with and has not acquired a taste for mulled wine (referred to as "glue line" or "glühwein"), a traditional drink at German Christmas markets. (Verbatim: "i've not yet acquired a taste for that i'll be honest... basically um that's yeah glue line")

8. She is familiar with and enjoys elements of German Christmas markets, such as bratwurst, roasted chestnuts, and giant sausages, which she associates with British "German Christmas markets." (Verbatim: "we always call them the german christmas markets... you'll get like roasted chestnuts roasted chestnuts mulled wine sausages")

9. She finds it difficult to function properly when half-awake, recalling a time she put her top on inside out and backwards. (Verbatim: "i wandered over to the bathroom to like brush my teeth and i looked in the mirror and i was like it wasn't just inside out it was like back to front as well")

10. She mentions having a dog that sometimes wakes her up, or at least dreams about it. (Verbatim: "my dog waking me up at one point i'm pretty certain or i dreamt it i don't know") [end of text]



